    "pareto_analysis": "At k=1 (3 KB) and k=2 (6 KB), compressing multi-clause arithmetic prompts loses intermediate clause boundaries, dropping Task-Calibrated accuracy from 96.0% to 72.0% (k=1) and 85.0% (k=2) and Unsupervised SVD accuracy from 61.0% to 48.0% (k=1). Conversely, expanding to k=8 (24 KB) and k=16 (48 KB) yields negligible accuracy gain (+0.0% to +1.0%) and +0.0021 cosine gain, while increasing CPU L12..19 compute time by 1.36x (k=8) and 2.11x (k=16) \u2014 causing k=16 FP16 CPU execution (254.3 ms) to overflow the 208.4 ms GPU overlap window. Thus k=4 (12 KB) sits squarely at the Pareto optimal knee."
